<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength on Archaeopteryx lithographica at 75 µm (Tithonian, 150.0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg system (a=0.112, b=0.836, Du=0.052, Dv=1.48, gamma=0.039, anisotropy 1.22, seed 3120) and the same 7.478e-05 m wavelength at 150.0 Ma. The wing window is now a full soft mask (fraction 0.080) and the critical mode is mixed onto that window at alpha 0.78, so vertical activator bars are readable on the vane. Grid FFT wavelength remains 12.00 cells versus 11.991 analytical (relative error 0.00072). Wing-transect 3-harmonic Pearson r = 0.9803, fundamental-only r = 0.807, nRMSE = 0.198, KS = 0.053. Equal-diffusion ablation std ratio = 0.00081. Neighbor predictions at the same dx: Anchiornis 95.33 µm (160.8 Ma), Microraptor 57.05 µm (120 Ma). Overall 87.2/100 (faithfulness 86.6, reproducibility 88.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 83, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/archaeopteryx_lithographica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 752917 B, 1496×924 px, artifact_sha256 4417000cdfb1483e9fba10d4ef922723b45a0827e244ce8785b4e1c6876757cb (sha256 4417000cdfb1483e9fba10d4ef922723b45a0827e244ce8785b4e1c6876757cb), spec_fingerprint 6913098e47054812a2f1cf896b7e10fbf923735b2080ce927a3087eecb641c84. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6913098e47054812a2f1cf896b7e10fbf923735b2080ce927a3087eecb641c84; artifact_sha256: 4417000cdfb1483e9fba10d4ef922723b45a0827e244ce8785b4e1c6876757cb; input_dataset_sha256: {archaeopteryx_lithographica_berlin_slab.jpg=2e307a2774e08571..., archaeopteryx_lithographica_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=32deca0baa44c4ef...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator. | Schnakenberg 1979: kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Prum and Williamson 2002: within-feather bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion class. | Carney 2012: Archaeopteryx feather melanosomes at roughly micrometre length. | Manning 2013 and Foth 2014: plumage pattern and pennaceous feathers at 150 Ma. | Li 2010 and Li 2012: Anchiornis colour and Microraptor iridescence.; reconstructed_in_script: Parameter tuple (a, b, Du, Dv, gamma, anisotropy) chosen so lambda_c = 7.478e-05 m. | Gamma shifts 0.024 and 0.067 for the Anchiornis and Microraptor predictions. | Quartic plus three harmonics fitted to the wing optical-density transect of the slab scan. | Pass-2 wing mix: alpha 0.78 of the critical mode inside the soft wing window.; transfer_boundary: The public-domain slab JPEG does not resolve 75 µm. The Pearson r is a scan-resolution transect fit, not a measured barbule spacing.; does_not_claim: That 74.78 µm was measured on this photograph. | That Anchiornis or Microraptor wavelengths were measured; they are gamma-transfer predictions. | A molecular identity for u and v.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved in Pass 2. Wing mix alpha is 0.78 inside the soft wing window; vertical bars are visible on the vane and cv_sim_similarity stayed 96.0.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved in Pass 2. The transect panel prints 3-harmonic r=0.9803 and fundamental r=0.807.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Resolved in Pass 2. The slab panel is titled with wing mask fraction 0.080.', 'status': 'resolved'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.72e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

