<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength on Archaeopteryx lithographica at 75 µm (Tithonian, 150.0 Ma) (Archaeopteryx lithographica)",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength on Archaeopteryx lithographica at 75 µm (Tithonian, 150.0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Archaeopteryx lithographica morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Archaeopteryx lithographica specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Archaeopteryx lithographica" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A molecular identity for u and v.",
        "does_not_claim: That 74.78 µm was measured on this photograph.",
        "does_not_claim: That Anchiornis or Microraptor wavelengths were measured; they are gamma-transfer predictions.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gamma shifts 0.024 and 0.067 for the Anchiornis and Microraptor predictions.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Parameter tuple (a, b, Du, Dv, gamma, anisotropy) chosen so lambda_c = 7.478e-05 m.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass-2 wing mix: alpha 0.78 of the critical mode inside the soft wing window.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Quartic plus three harmonics fitted to the wing optical-density transect of the slab scan.",
        "reported_in_source: Carney 2012: Archaeopteryx feather melanosomes at roughly micrometre length.",
        "reported_in_source: Li 2010 and Li 2012: Anchiornis colour and Microraptor iridescence.",
        "reported_in_source: Manning 2013 and Foth 2014: plumage pattern and pennaceous feathers at 150 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Prum and Williamson 2002: within-feather bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion class.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator.",
        "transfer_boundary: The public-domain slab JPEG does not resolve 75 µm. The Pearson r is a scan-resolution transect fit, not a measured barbule spacing." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Archaeopteryx lithographica (Late Jurassic (Tithonian, 150.0 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Archaeopteryx" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/archaeopteryx_lithographica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Archaeopteryx lithographica; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator. | Schnakenberg 1979: kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Prum and Williamson 2002: within-feather bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion class. | Carney 2012: Archaeopteryx feather melanosomes at roughly micrometre length. | Manning 2013 and Foth 2014: plumage pattern and pennaceous feathers at 150 Ma. | Li 2010 and Li 2012: Anchiornis colour and Microraptor iridescence.; reconstructed_in_script: Parameter tuple (a, b, Du, Dv, gamma, anisotropy) chosen so lambda_c = 7.478e-05 m. | Gamma shifts 0.024 and 0.067 for the Anchiornis and Microraptor predictions. | Quartic plus three harmonics fitted to the wing optical-density transect of the slab scan. | Pass-2 wing mix: alpha 0.78 of the critical mode inside the soft wing window.; transfer_boundary: The public-domain slab JPEG does not resolve 75 µm. The Pearson r is a scan-resolution transect fit, not a measured barbule spacing.; does_not_claim: That 74.78 µm was measured on this photograph. | That Anchiornis or Microraptor wavelengths were measured; they are gamma-transfer predictions. | A molecular identity for u and v.]; phenomenon_size: 58 µm (5.838e-05 m, log10=-4.234 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 58 µm to 13.1 cm): 58 µm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-bioelectric-polarity, 182 µm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-vertex-packing, 2.9 mm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength, 5.8 mm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-clock-wavefront, 1.3 cm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-morphogen-condensation, 1.6 cm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-elastic-buckling, 1.8 cm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-flux-canalization, 2.6 cm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-branching-tree" ;
